1785543344346526	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy1AQ		item.comment	bn-2felx	{"body":"Added a 56-line orientation block to AGENTS.md above the edict:managed-start marker (managed block byte-identical, sha256 47447da2 before and after). Three subsections: 'What Continuum is' (Model/Program/Proof planes, protected Intent Contract, evidence as sole currency, agent-native but never trusted; notes current design-and-scaffold state), 'Where things live' (notes/plan dossier layout, crates/ = plan §20 membership enforced by tools/check_crate_boundaries.py, lean/ T0/T1 kernel-checked, just check as the gate), and 'Key invariants' (8 items, each with a source pointer): no self-certification (INV-004 + plan §20 dependency rules), typed inconclusiveness (INV-008), protected intent (INV-001/011), no ambient nondeterminism + deterministic artifacts (INV-005, ADR-0003, Cargo.toml/Justfile --locked), epochs are content identities and the three schema identities are distinct (plan §4.6, ADR-0018, schemas/README.md), schemas decide not prose (INV-003), unsafe_code forbidden workspace-wide with no override (Cargo.toml [workspace.lints.rust]), RFC beats plan (plan §25). Picked these eight because each one can silently invalidate a code change: they cover what you may not depend on, what you may not return, what you may not edit, what you may not call, and which document wins. Pointer to plan §2 for the full INV-001..018 set. Verified: git diff is one hunk at line 8 (+56/-0), entirely above the marker; dossier validator (uv run --with jsonschema python3 tools/validate_dossier.py) exits 0 with status pass, program_status ready; git status clean apart from AGENTS.md. Committed e77d9fa."}	blake3:t2PREujf-OrLpbT4Mb152zq9eVpGP5n6QgYQP5BKdUA
