1785543525190086	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy1gQ		item.comment	bn-zr81	{"body":"PR-4A exit verified independently from a clean tree (2026-07-31): lake clean && lake build succeeded (19 jobs, no errors, no 'declaration uses sorry' warnings); scripts/axiom-manifest.sh --check reported 'axiom manifest is up to date'; lake env lean --version = 4.32.1 matching the pinned lean-toolchain; fresh sorry/admit/axiom/native_decide/set_option sweep over Continuum/ and Continuum.lean found nothing (sole tree-wide hit is the word 'axiom' in an AxiomManifest.lean doc comment, tooling outside the library target); lake env lean Continuum.lean exited 0. All 68 manifest rows carry an empty axiom list and all 68 names resolve to real theorems in the built environment (no dangling rows). 18 rows spot-verified individually with #print axioms, at least one from each of the 11 rung items, every one printing 'does not depend on any axioms' and matching its manifest row. An environment-wide collectAxioms sweep over all 204 theorems in the Continuum modules found 29 axiom-dependent, all propext only, never Classical.choice / Quot.sound / sorryAx; exactly 2 are authored claims (Continuum.cancel_step_decreases_rank, Continuum.Examples.DieHard.solution_ends_with_four_gallons), both pre-existing and both outside the T0/T1 ladder as documented, the other 27 compiler-generated. Rung coverage: all 4 RFC 0012 T0 rung items and all 5 T1 rung items map to at least one manifest row under the RFC's exact wording — zero gaps; the manifest additionally carries two T0 groups the RFC does not enumerate (checker trusted base, Die Hard instantiation), which are additive. Exit recorded in lean/README.md ('PR-4A exit evidence') and the START_HERE PR 4a Exit line annotated '(delivered: bn-zr81)'; traceability regenerated (PR-4A and PR-4A-EXIT flipped to satisfied) and validate_dossier.py returned status pass."}	blake3:W3YWBInop8tBmDiBgCxDFO6l17sx3LwennLSBvYiWbE
