1785544027957626	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy5gQ		item.comment	bn-1rxrr	{"body":"Added mise.toml at workspace root (bn-1rxrr): pins just=1.57.0, uv=0.11.18, and elan=4.2.3 via the ubi backend (ubi:leanprover/elan; elan has no default-registry entry). Rust and Lean intentionally NOT pinned in mise.toml -- Rust stays rustup + rust-toolchain.toml (bn-2b8w); Lean stays lean/lean-toolchain (leanprover/lean4:v4.32.1) selected by elan, layering documented as mise -> elan -> pinned toolchain in mise.toml comments and a new README.md '#### Toolchain' subsection under Deterministic builds. Verified: mise config ls / mise ls resolved the manifest cleanly; ran a real (non-destructive) 'mise install' -- installed just and elan into mise's own installs dir (~/.local/share/mise/installs/...), confirmed by byte-identical md5sum that ~/.elan/bin/elan and ~/.elan/toolchains/ (v4.25.1/4.26.0-rc2/4.28.0/4.32.1) were untouched; uv already satisfied by the existing global 'latest' install. just check passes end-to-end in the workspace (status: pass) both before and after the README edit. Did not touch Justfile, notes/, or .bones/. Concern: mise emitted 'deprecated [ubi]: use the github backend instead (e.g., github:owner/repo); removed in mise 2027.1.0' -- ubi:leanprover/elan works today and matches the syntax the bone directive specified, but this repo will need a follow-up to migrate to github:leanprover/elan before that removal date. Committed in workspace as 'chore: mise.toml for tool dependencies (bn-1rxrr)' (c8e3daf); not merged, no bone-state change per instructions."}	blake3:tJjVUdU2NHr6b72zKgeIYHPgYkFC3dYO05TQ1MCeMRo
